      "content": "Here are some talking points for your field reps: \n\nCardioZen's side-effect profile is comparable to the competitor, but with a more comprehensive patient support system in place, allowing for earlier intervention and reduced long-term risks. Our data shows potential patients are more likely to withdraw from treatment due to side effects with the competitor. \nCardioZen's active ingredient, rilminidase, is designed to target specific effects rather than treating all symptoms simultaneously, which may lead to more severe side effects in some patients. \nCardioZen won the FDA's Breakthrough Therapy designation for this use case, demonstrating the unprecedented potential benefits to patients, as well as suggesting a more targeted and effective approach.",
